BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Am Nevenka
DTSTART:20250521T200000Z
DTEND:20250521T220500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T200000Z
UID:ejwY3MthTk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nNevenka Fernández\, the town’
 s finance councilor\, is relentlessly pursued by the mayor\, a man used to
  always getting what he wants politically and personally. Nevenka decides 
 to report him\, turning her courageous fight into Spain’s first #MeToo c
 ase. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/i-am-nevenka\n\nAlso p
 laying at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Fri 23 May\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baby Doe
DTSTART:20250521T224500Z
DTEND:20250522T003500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T224500Z
UID:boGHR3eOBU
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nNearly 30 years after Gail aband
 oned her newborn son in the woods and returned to her conservative Christi
 an life\, the police came and arrested her for infanticide. From Tribeca-w
 inning documentarian Jessica Earnshaw (Hulu’s “Jacinta”). Director J
 essica Earnshaw and co-producer John Rudolf scheduled to attend. Sponsored
  by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/baby-doe
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Safe House
DTSTART:20250522T013000Z
DTEND:20250522T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T013000Z
UID:joC9jNrBmv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nIn this sincere and impeccably ar
 t-directed Wes Anderson-esque film based on Christophe Boltanski’s memoi
 r “La Cache\,” a nine-year-old boy and his quirky\, artistic family ex
 perience the turbulence of 1968 Paris from the relative safety of their mu
 ltigenerational home. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-s
 afe-house\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Thu 22 May\, 6:
 00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hanami
DTSTART:20250522T040000Z
DTEND:20250522T055000Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T040000Z
UID:IHEaNxABPn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nWeaving between the natural and m
 agical\, Nana lives on a remote volcanic island from where everybody leave
 s. Left by her mother soon after birth\, she will spend her life trying to
  find the right answer to the lingering question in her mind and soul: Sho
 uld she stay or should she go? Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/hanami\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Riefenstahl
DTSTART:20250522T193000Z
DTEND:20250522T214000Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T193000Z
UID:vsZ2HGm26r
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nA gripping portrait of controver
 sial filmmaker and propagandist Leni Riefenstahl (The Triumph of the Will)
 \, who despite all evidence to the contrary still maintained she was not c
 omplicit in the atrocities carried out by the Third Reich. Sponsored by:\n
 \nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/riefenstahl
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Everybody Loves Touda
DTSTART:20250522T221500Z
DTEND:20250523T001000Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T221500Z
UID:RAFdx0wFc6
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nTouda dreams of being a sheikha\
 , or traditional Moroccan folk singer. But in a culture where female perfo
 rmers are as often eroticized and stigmatized as venerated\, what does it 
 really mean to be loved? Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/ev
 erybody-loves-touda\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 
 (Fri 23 May\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Visions
DTSTART:20250523T013000Z
DTEND:20250523T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T013000Z
UID:aphaQ90buS
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nFrom tying the knot\, to settling
  a score\, to appreciating unrecognized icons in our midst\, these shorts 
 explore our region’s creative spirit and talented filmmaking community. 
 Study your local film trivia before attending the screening because the Se
 attle Film Society will be giving away tickets to one of their upcoming ev
 ents! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sound-visions-x39746\
 n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beef
DTSTART:20250523T043000Z
DTEND:20250523T060500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T043000Z
UID:yt4yLSRtAa
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nLati\, a first-generation Malian 
 migrant\, turns to rap to overcome the death of her father. Determined to 
 overcome her fears of performing and to confront her mom’s opposition\, 
 a new world opens up when she learns how to tap into her frustration and a
 nger to create empowering\, liberating rhymes. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/festival/beef
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Kingdom
DTSTART:20250523T200000Z
DTEND:20250523T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T200000Z
UID:WGh2ZGWUpG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 108 mins (1h48m)\n\nWhen an underground war breaks o
 ut between nationalist groups and crime families\, a Corsican mobster and 
 his daughter must go on the run\, bringing them closer together and drawin
 g her into his world. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-k
 ingdom\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (Wed 21 May\,
  7:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Suburban Fury
DTSTART:20250523T223000Z
DTEND:20250524T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T223000Z
UID:MJTpdPKcuk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nLocal documentarian Robinson Dev
 or (Zoo\, Pow Wow) returns to SIFF with this outré and probing biography 
 of Sara Jane Moore\, the FBI informant and single mother who tried to assa
 ssinate President Gerald Ford in 1975\, as told in her own words. Director
  Robinson Devor\, producer Jason Reid\, executive producer/head archivist 
 Bob Fink\, and co-producer Matt Levinthal scheduled to attend. RSVP to joi
 n Seattle Documentary Association for a happy hour celebrating local docum
 entary filmmaking at Sound Hotel directly before the film. Limited space a
 vailable. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/suburban-fury\n\n
 Also playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Wed 21 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Time Travel Is Dangerous
DTSTART:20250524T013000Z
DTEND:20250524T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T013000Z
UID:ewnbcbjVbT
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nWhat would you do if a time-trave
 l bumper car fell into your lap? If you’re Ruth and Megan of North Londo
 n\, you use it to find and sell antiques at your vintage shop\, of course\
 , regardless of the consequences reverberating across time and space. Dire
 ctor Chris Reading and co-writers/producers Hillary and Anna-Elizabeth Sh
 akespeare scheduled to attend. Satiate your love for sci-fi with tickets t
 o MoPOP\, our trivia giveaway at the May 23 screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/festival/time-travel-is-dangerous\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cin
 ema Uptown House 2 (Sat 24 May\, 12:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Spirit Cabinet
DTSTART:20250524T043000Z
DTEND:20250524T062000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T043000Z
UID:UfwEKRcLj3
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nWithin the spirit cabinet\, disco
 ver messages from the beyond\, supernatural terrors\, and an unimaginably 
 creepy cabaret.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-spirit-cabinet\n\nFil
 m is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twinless
DTSTART:20250524T193000Z
DTEND:20250524T212000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T193000Z
UID:ZLr6R6OMDv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nIn this Portland-set dark comedy
  from James Sweeney (2019’s crowdpleasing Straight Up)\, two men (Dylan 
 O’Brien and Sweeney) trauma-bond at a support group for people who have 
 lost their twin. Winner of the Sundance 2025 US Dramatic Audience Award. D
 irector James Sweeney scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festiv
 al/twinless\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Sun 25 
 May\, 7:15 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cat Town\, USA
DTSTART:20250524T223000Z
DTEND:20250524T235500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T223000Z
UID:4W4ZjV5sOH
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 73 mins (1h13m)\n\nIn this feel-good doc expanded fr
 om a SIFF 2019 short\, filmmaker Jonathan Napolitano snuggles up with Bruc
 e and Terry Jenkins\, an aging Floridian couple who’ve decided to spend 
 their last days running a retirement home for senior and aging cats. Direc
 tor Jonathan Napolitano and producer James Gannon scheduled to attend. Ins
 pired to save a cat yourself? Seattle Area Feline Rescue will be onsite Ma
 y 22 to share information about their wonderful adoptable kitties! Sponsor
 ed by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/cat-town-usa\n\nAlso playing at:\n
   • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (Thu 22 May\, 7:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also be
 ing streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DJ Ahmet
DTSTART:20250525T010000Z
DTEND:20250525T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T010000Z
UID:MeWg9BTxUS
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nFifteen-year-old shepherd Ahmet r
 ebels against his conservative North Macedonian farming village when he ge
 ts a taste of electronic dance music in this heartwarming dramedy\, winner
  of the World Cinema – Audience Award Prize at Sundance 2025. Sponsored 
 by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/dj-ahmet\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • A
 MC Pacific Place 11 (Sun 25 May\, 11:00 AM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rebuilding
DTSTART:20250525T033000Z
DTEND:20250525T051500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T033000Z
UID:Iy74Mhr2Oh
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nIn Max Walker-Silverman’s tende
 r follow-up to A Love Song (SIFF 2022 Golden Space Needle Award for Best 
 Performance)\, Josh O’Connor (Challengers) stars as a Coloradan cowboy w
 ho reconnects with his daughter and ex-wife after a wildfire takes his fam
 ily ranch.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/rebuilding\n\nAlso playing at:
 \n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Sun 25 May\, 6:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tales From the Magic Garden
DTSTART:20250525T180000Z
DTEND:20250525T192500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T180000Z
UID:sMLREA0LXf
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 71 mins (1h11m)\n\nIn this stop motion marvel from t
 he Czech Republic based on the stories of author Arnošt Goldflam (“The 
 Zookeeper’s Wife”)\, three young children visit their late grandmother
 ’s house\, where they take turns spinning fantastical tales to better un
 derstand loss\, compassion\, and empathy. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.sif
 f.net/festival/tales-from-the-magic-garden
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Anka: His Way
DTSTART:20250525T200000Z
DTEND:20250525T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T200000Z
UID:g0IX1j6Mhv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nHe faced it all\, stood tall\, an
 d did it his way. Get the inside scoop on the life and career of Paul Anka
 \, the Canadian-born son of immigrants who rocketed to the top of the char
 ts not just as a teen heartthrob\, but as the songwriter of some of Americ
 a’s greatest standards. Director John Maggio scheduled to attend May 23 
 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/paul-anka-his-wa
 y\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Fri 23 May\, 3:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slanted
DTSTART:20250525T223000Z
DTEND:20250526T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T223000Z
UID:SWLL7JjnNO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 104 mins (1h44m)\n\nChinese American teen Joan Huang
  just wants to fit in at her high school\, but when she hastily undergoes 
 an experimental medical procedure to become Caucasian\, the consequences c
 ould be devastating in this biting speculative fiction satire. SXSW Grand 
 Jury winner. Director Amy Wang scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/festival/slanted\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (
 Sat 24 May\, 9:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
